  ],
  "grid_title": "TYPES OF JOINT",
  "why": "Ball and socket: a round head in a cup, moves every way (hip, shoulder). Hinge: bends one way like a door (knee, elbow). Pivot: one bone turns around another (top two neck bones, turning your head). Saddle: two curved surfaces (base of the thumb). Condyloid: an oval bump fits an oval cup, up-down and side to side (big knuckles, wrist). Plane: flat surfaces that slide a little (small wrist bones).",
